    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0627" n="525" xml:id="pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2489</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice President of the Continental &amp; Commercial
                        Trust &amp; Savings Bank of Chicago</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Abbott</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                        1919</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We hand you herewith fourth original of
                        agreement<anchor n="22" xml:id="d485-f1"/> entered into between the Republic
                    of China and this Bank, dated October 20, 1919, which we would ask you to read
                    and place in your files.</p>
                <p>While not mentioned in the contract, it is set forth in separate memoranda, and
                    is distinctly understood by Messrs. Hsu Un Yuen and Yung Kwai, who signed the
                    contract on behalf of the Chinese Government, that the same shall not become
                    effective until the contract has been approved by the Executive Committee of
                    this Bank.</p>
                <p>Yours respectfully,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Continental and Commercial<lb/>Trust and Savings
                        Bank of Chicago</hi><lb/>By <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Jay
                            Abbott</hi></signed>, <hi rendition="#italic">Vice
                    President</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
